  "hms_surface": "hms-server memory API (remember, recall k=5 hybrid with embedding, get, forget ids + purge)",
  "agent_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731 via OpenRouter, provider pinned to DeepSeek (no fallbacks), reasoning off, temperature 0",
  "judge_model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731 via OpenRouter, provider pinned to DeepSeek (no fallbacks), reasoning off, temperature 0",
  "embedding_model": "openai/text-embedding-3-small via OpenRouter",
  "model_notes": "The published DeepSeek rows record agent deepseek-deepseek-v4-flash-0731 and judge alias deepseek-flash (rejudged 2026-09-24, before deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 existed). The paper text names DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash. The DeepSeek API account was unfunded, so both roles used the dated 0731 snapshot through OpenRouter. same_day_rag is Bemula's own Naive RAG baseline rerun with these models as a drift control.",
  "guarantee_mapping": {
    "engine": "a purged fact is never returned by recall and the store matches one that never held it (docs/memory-api/README.md, tests/forget_equivalence.rs); checked on every probe as purged_ids_returned_by_recall",
    "adapter_policy": "request detection (regex screen + agent-model classifier) and which stored facts a request covers (agent-model review of every stored fact)",
    "outside_any_storage_guarantee": "F4 inferential targets and multihop attacks answerable from facts never covered; agent-model guesses on enumeration (yes/no) and jailbreak probes"
  },
  "deviations": [
    "Judge snapshot inferred: the authors' run_meta records the alias deepseek-flash (rejudged 2026-09-24, before deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017 existed); the paper text says DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash. Models are served through OpenRouter (a third party) pinned to DeepSeek's deployment."
  ],
  "run_history": "A first run was stopped and not published: OpenRouter ignored Bemula's DeepSeek thinking switch (reasoning was on, provider unpinned), a failed forget-review call was treated as flagging nothing, the request screen missed typographic apostrophes, and its log could not separate control and forget copies. The adapter fixes are error handling only; prompts, k and batch sizes are unchanged.",
